    a: 'Not yet — not one you can buy. A real tan means your own cells building brown eumelanin, and that has been done topically in the lab: forskolin darkened pale mice, and small-molecule SIK inhibitors darkened human skin samples. But neither has become an approved or marketed product, and no over-the-counter cream has been shown to switch on genuine melanin in human skin. The tanning lotions on shelves today do something completely different.',
