  <h2>The honest bottom line</h2>
  <p>
    If you want darker skin today without UV, the only real option is a DHA
    self-tanner — and it is a cosmetic surface stain, not a tan, with no meaningful
    sun protection and no connection to your pigment cells. The genuine prize, a
    cream that switches on your own protective eumelanin, is real science and has
    been demonstrated in human skin samples through the melanocortin/cAMP pathway —
    but it remains a laboratory result, not a product on a shelf. The gap between
    the two is almost entirely about the skin barrier and about proving such a
    thing safe. Until that gap is closed, the elegant truth stands: the switch for a
    real tan exists in your skin, and we can now reach it from the outside in the
    lab — but not yet, and not safely, from a bottle. For the injected route and its
    documented risks, see the <a href="/melanotan">melanotan explainer</a>; for the
    pigment switch itself, <a href="/receptors/mc1r">MC1R</a>.
  </p>

